{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_izheqftrlt7gvnpgq7znfxk7igt6vulsnalvbdvmjju7cylaobsa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four phases complete; **the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte**.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src` is one 43-line translation unit exporting exactly two symbols, `run(int)` and `driver(int)`, which mutate a file-scope `static house_t the_house = {2, 5, 2.5}` and `printf` its state. No branches, no error returns, no pointers/enums in the public API, no `#ifdef`.\n\n## Phase A artifacts (`translation/`)\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` diff is **empty**. Both `.so`s export `driver` and `run`; note `run` is *not* in `driver.h` but is non-`static`, so it is public and the Rust exports it. All six C `static` internals stay unexported on both sides.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — mechanical grep proves **0** occurrences of `return`/`assert`/`if`/`NULL`/`malloc`/error enum. Both functions are `void f(int)`, so there is no error channel and no rejecting input. Table records that as 2 rows + 6 generic FFI-boundary rows (null-pointer, zero/oversized length, one-past-range, out-of-range enum) each marked applicable or `N/A` with the reason from the source.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 20 rows over the real axes: both entry points (incl. the low-level `run`, not just `driver`), argument shapes incl. `INT_MAX`/`INT_MIN`/exact-boundary landings, and *persistent-global-state sequences* (the call sequence is part of the input here).\n\n## Phases B–D results\n`tests/harness/mod.rs` + `tests/configs.rs` + `tests/errors.rs`: **29 tests, all passing** under release and debug, and under both feature configurations (`Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so default and `--no-default-features` are the complete set). `run_all.sh` automates build → symbol diff → tests across all combos.\n\nBoth `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` and only their exported symbols are called. Since `the_house` persists, each test copies both `.so`s to unique inodes so `dlopen` yields pristine state, then replays the identical op sequence against each and compares captured `stdout` (via `dup2` on fd 1 + `fflush(NULL)`, serialized by a mutex). Randomized rows use fixed-seed SplitMix64.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n1. **Real harness bug found and fixed.** `cargo test` does *not* relink the `cdylib` (integration tests don't link it), so my first green run was testing a **stale `.so`**. I proved it by injecting `bathrooms: 2.6` — the test still passed. After an explicit `cargo build --release` the same injection failed loudly with a byte offset. The harness now refuses to run if `libdriver.so` is older than any `src/*.rs` (and likewise for the C `.so` vs `c_src/src/*.c`), so this can never silently pass again.\n2. **The one genuine correctness risk is signed overflow.** `the_house.bedrooms += extra_bedrooms` is UB in C; gcc wraps two's-complement, and the Rust's `wrapping_add` matches. Verified at `INT_MAX`, `INT_MIN`, exact and one-past boundary landings, and under repeated wrapping (40 consecutive `INT_MAX` adds).\n\nNo divergences were found, so no fixes to `src/lib.rs` were needed. `c_src/` is unmodified apart from the generated `build/` directory the task instructed me to create.\n\nCaveat: crates.io is unreachable from the sandbox, so all cargo commands use `--offline` against the already-cached `libloading 0.8.9`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2335,"cache_read_input_tokens":61394,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2335,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"326e65a2-d440-4c4f-baf0-85d2549d617d","uuid":"68ae3440-150e-4a7b-9aaa-a6ee7b47fc17","timestamp":"2026-09-05T04:17:33.969Z"}
